# Copy this file to .env.local, which is gitignored, and fill in the two
# keys. The rest is set for the shared backend and Typesense. `npm run web`
# from src/ reads the file, and prints one line at startup if anything is
# missing. Step by step: docs/run-locally.md.
#
# No VITE_ prefix on purpose: Vite exposes only VITE_ variables to the client
# code, so these two cannot end up in the bundle. The dev server is the proxy
# that sets X-API-Key. The key works only for the backend it was made for;
# against the stack on your machine it is KA_API_URL=http://localhost:8080 and
# the key from there.
KA_API_URL=https://test.rag.digdir.cloud
KA_API_KEY=

# Which corpus live mode asks. The VITE_ prefix is on purpose: these are names
# of datasets, not secrets, and they must reach the client code.
#
# Both or neither. The backend builds the dataset scope only when it has both,
# so one alone is dropped there and the answer comes from the default corpus
# anyway. The client therefore drops a lone value and says so in the console.
# Without them the backend picks the corpus itself, and the filter panel has no
# dataset to count.
VITE_KA_TENANT=public-sector-knowledge
VITE_KA_DATASET_CONFIG_KEY=kudos
VITE_KA_DATASETS=kudos=Kudos|dokumenter fra kudos.dfo.no

# The MCP tool live asks. Without it, it is headless-rag's,
# builtin.agent-rag-agent__agent-rag-graph-bundled, and the conversations are
# made at the agent the tool belongs to. Not a secret. Against genki:
#
#   VITE_KA_TOOL=kunnskapsassistenten__default

# Typesense, for the facets in the filter panel (server/facets.ts) and the
# excerpts in the sources panel (server/excerpts.ts). Read by the dev server
# and the server, never by the client. The key is a search key with access to
# the collections, never the admin key. The collections are written
# "dataset=collection;…": the documents in KA_FACET_COLLECTIONS and the chunks
# in KA_CHUNK_COLLECTIONS. See docs/deploy.md.
TYPESENSE_URL=https://typesense-test.digdir.cloud:443
TYPESENSE_API_KEY=
KA_FACET_COLLECTIONS=kudos=KUDOS_preprod_v4_documents_ab897fbdedfa
KA_CHUNK_COLLECTIONS=kudos=KUDOS_preprod_v4_chunks_ab897fbdedfa

# The fields in the filter panel per dataset, "dataset=dimension:field[:type]|…;…"
# (shared/filterFields.ts). Without them the facets come back empty. The links
# to the documents per dataset, "dataset=numberTemplate|uuidTemplate"
# (src/api/documentUrls.ts).
VITE_KA_FILTER_FIELDS=kudos=documentType:type|organisation:orgs_long|year:concerned_years:integer
VITE_KA_DOCUMENT_URLS=kudos=https://kudos.dfo.no/documents/{doc_num}|https://kudos.dfo.no/dokument/{doc_num}

# VITE_API_MODE is NOT here. Every Vite server from the same checkout reads
# the same .env.local, so a mode put in the file applies to everyone running
# in this tree, and none of them asked for it. Without it, it is live in
# development and bff in a production build. Set it on the command line for
# the one run that needs something else:
#
#   VITE_API_MODE=bff npm run dev
#
# mock is the tests' mode: playwright.config.ts and vitest set it themselves.
# A value that is not live, bff or mock stops the dev server and the build.
#
# In bff mode (VITE_API_MODE=bff) the proxy goes only to the BFF in
# digdir/kunnskapsassistenten, which holds its own key. KA_API_URL and
# KA_API_KEY above are not read then. The default is :8788. See
# docs/bff-modus.md.
#
#   KA_BFF_URL=http://localhost:8788

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The test environment (server/, Dockerfile). Does not apply to `npm run dev`,
# which uses the Vite proxy and the variables at the top.
#
# Same split and same reason: DIGDIR_API_KEY has no VITE_ prefix, because it
# must never reach the client code. The server sets it on the call.
#
#   PORT=8787
#   KA_MODE=live                              # live | mock
#   DIGDIR_API_BASE=http://localhost:8080
#   DIGDIR_API_KEY=
#   KA_USER_ID_FROM=browser                   # browser | platform
#
# platform only behind Container Apps' sign-in, which sets it itself. See
# «Innlogging» in docs/deploy.md.
#
#   KA_ACCESS_SECRET=
#
# The shared secret in the link ?secret=. Empty = no gate. At least 24
# characters. See «Delt hemmelighet» in docs/deploy.md.
#
# The corpus variables are read by the server and written to the client in
# /config.js, so one image can run both mock and live. See docs/deploy.md.
#
#   VITE_KA_DATASETS=norquad-docs=Wikipedia (NorQuAD)|351 artikler;kudos-pilot=Kudos-pilot
